# Phase 18 admin query key-filter parity — 2026-10-21T14:10:44Z

Branch: `phase/18-phase-18-compatibility-closure`
Pinned Java dependency: `org.apache.rocketmq:rocketmq-client:5.5.1`
Pinned source commit: `efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9`

- Compared `MqClientAdminImpl.filterMessages` with both Rust query paths. Java
  uses Apache Commons `StringUtils.isNotBlank` (JDK
  `Character.isWhitespace`) and `String.split(" ")`; Rust previously used
  Unicode `trim()` in the direct wrapper and did not reject whitespace-only
  keys in the cross-Broker merge. It also dropped all empty split tokens,
  including interior ones.
- Added invoked Java cases for an empty query key matching an interior empty
  token but not a trailing token, NBSP, em-space, U+0085 and U+001C. Updated the
  Rust fixture comparison to cover all query cases.
- Added one Java-compatible key matcher shared by direct Broker filtering and
  cross-Broker merging. It uses the pinned `Character.isWhitespace` codepoint
  set and Java's trailing-empty-token removal while retaining interior tokens.
- Added unit assertions for the Java whitespace and split boundaries.
